A||||3||Snowball||anybody on how to install dew wipers||||8||
Z||000000||Snowball||06-05-2001||12:16 AM||||got new dew wipers and I went to insatall them. Only problem is I was told that I had to remove the outer skin. is that true? I rteplaced tohe inter ones but wasn't ready to pull the outer skin. Any help would be appreciated||||reg||8
Z||000001||Tigger||06-05-2001||01:00 AM||||No, you don't have to remove the outer door skin, just have to remove the interior panel and stamped trim pieces along the top of the door to get to the screws.  I replaced mine when I had my windows completely out so it was easy.  <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com" TARGET=_blank>www.rodneydickman.com</A>  sells a dew strip tool that I've heard works and you don't have to remove the glass.<p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 06-05-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfixit58||06-05-2001||07:48 AM||||You may want to try a search on "dew wipes". This topic comes up frequently ant you should find plenty of information. Personally, I prefer to remove the door panel and unbolt the window tracks. This allows the window to slide forward and back to gain access to the two screws in the middle. To realign the window, simply put the bolts back in their original location. To make the bolt locations more obvious, use a marker to trace a circle around them before you remove them. <P><P>------------------<BR>Roy :D<BR>87 GT  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG"> ||||reg||3
Z||000003||Bob Englert||06-05-2001||12:34 PM||||The Michigan Fiero club website has a good writeup on dew wipe replacement at <A HREF="http://www.michiganfieroclub.org/dewstrip.pdf" TARGET=_blank>http://www.michiganfieroclub.org/dewstrip.pdf</A> <P>The file is in Adobe Acrobat format so you will need to download an acrobat reader if you don't have it now.  Rodney's dew wipe tool is helpful but you can make your own with a small racheting screwdriver attachment or angled Phillips head screwdriver.  <P>It takes forever (it seems) to replace the first one, it gets easier with practice (doesn't everything)!<P>Good luck...<P><BR>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl<p>[This message has been edited by Bob Englert (edited 06-05-2001).]||||reg||1
